# .git_msg
#
# This file is OPTIONAL. It is a free-form commit message hint used by
# contributors and tooling to pre-fill or suggest a commit subject line.
#
# Purpose:
#   - Provide a suggested commit message for the current change set.
#   - Help keep commit subjects consistent with the repo's conventions.
#
# Format:
#   - Plain UTF-8 text.
#   - First line: a conventional-commit style subject, e.g.
#       feat: add recovery FAQ section with accessible accordion
#       fix: clarify .git_msg optional
#   - Optional following lines: additional body/context.
#   - No secrets, tokens, or credentials may be committed here.
#
# Notes:
#   - Absence of this file is valid; nothing in CI or hooks requires it.
#   - It does not affect runtime behavior.
#
# Suggested message for the current change set:
feat: add recovery FAQ section with accessible accordion
